      "id": "GO:0019985",
      "isObsolete": false,
      "name": "translesion synthesis",
      "definition": {
        "text": "The replication of damaged DNA by synthesis across a lesion in the template strand; a specialized DNA polymerase or replication complex inserts a defined nucleotide across from the lesion which allows DNA synthesis to continue beyond the lesion. This process can be mutagenic depending on the damaged nucleotide and the inserted nucleotide.",
